    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37658" root="لخب" body-key="l">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَخَبَ</span></b>  <i>He slapped</i> a person; <i>struck</i> him
<i>with the open hand.</i> (K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَخَبَ</span>, aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَخَبَ</span></b>  and 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَخُبَ</span></b> ,
(inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَخْبٌ</span>, TA,) <i>Inivit</i> feminam: (Kr, K:)
but the word commonly known, related by
Yaakoob and others, is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَخَبَ</span>. (ISd.)

